:: the_frontier__veilwood [the_frontier]
<!-- harness:meta
location: veilwood
-->

The Veilwood is wrong.

The trees you remember from your mapping expeditions are gone, replaced by darker growth: bark like wet leather, leaves that hang in spirals. The Serpentine runs through the center of the wood now, wide and slow, and its water is the same blue-black as your ink.

You stop to fill your canteen. The water tastes of parchment and ozone. You can feel it in your teeth.

And then you notice: the trees on the far bank are growing in rows. Not naturally. In the pattern of your map's ink grain. The forest is becoming your map.

You hear something moving through the undergrowth. Not an animal. The sound is rhythmic, deliberate. Footsteps.

